# Code owners (blueprint S9; release checklist item 5).
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request
# touches. The public repository, github.com/JeremiahJRRoss/librerun,
# belongs to its maintainer's personal account, which has no teams, so
# every rule names that one user, @JeremiahJRRoss. The handle is written
# in by scripts/resolve_public_owner.sh, and a placeholder put back is
# refused: `scripts/prepare_public_repo.sh` will not prepare a tree that
# carries one unless told to out loud.
#
# Where that user cannot review, in any repository but the public one,
# GitHub ignores these lines: they route nowhere and block nothing.

# Everything, unless a later rule wins.
*                           @JeremiahJRRoss

# The release machinery: a change here changes what a release carries
# and the checks that stand in its way. None of it publishes (L37).
